 "consequencesInTheShippedBeautyPath": [
  "refract(-V, N, 1/ior) with N = 0 returns eta * incident -- a scaled view ray with NO dependence on the surface, so the refraction displacement carries perspective only.",
  "projectedNormalOffset = vec2(N.x, -N.y) * ... = exactly zero. This term was described in OpticsConfigV4 as 'the only term that tracks the surface normal directly'.",
  "facing = saturate(dot(N, V)) = 0, so fresnel = pow(1, 5) = 1 -- saturated everywhere, which is what the flat fresnel view shows."
 ],
 "explainsGate005": "GATE-005 recorded that the refraction-offset debug view moves at most 2 of 255 levels while the same change moved 34.9% of beauty pixels, and treated that view as unsound. The audit gives the mechanism: projectedNormalOffset is identically zero, so that view was reporting a real zero rather than failing to report. The anomaly is explained, not merely reproduced.",
 "notFixedHere": "\u00a7\u4e09 forbids repair during the audit. The finding is carried into the O4 attribution and makes \u00a7\u4e03.E eligible for consideration -- it does not select it."
}